<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-119] SparkILoop loadFiles is called before binder initialization</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-119</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In SparkInterpreter, method open(), the call to SparkILoop loadFiles method is performed before putting &apos;sqlc&apos;, &apos;sc&apos;, &apos;z&apos; and &apos;out&apos; into the binder object.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This means that if you have any scala init script you want to pass to Spark through the &apos;args&apos; interpreter option (e.g.: args=&quot;-i init.scala&quot;), in those init script you won&apos;t have access to any Spark&apos;s context.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Having access to &apos;sc&apos; or &apos;sqlc&apos; is useful to customize context initialization, like for example, adding custom UDFs to sql context.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12838823">ZEPPELIN-119</key>
            <summary>SparkILoop loadFiles is called before binder initialization</summary>
